The catamorphism is monotone. If a sharp neighbourhood is related to a target neighbourhood, a smaller sharp neighbourhood is contained in the source, and a larger target neighbourhood contains the target, then the smaller source is related to the larger target.

The argument inducts on the relation. At the master, the larger target must be the master, and every sharp neighbourhood is related to the master. At a zero embedding, a smaller sharp neighbourhood contained in a zero embedding is the zero embedding of a smaller neighbourhood, and monotonicity of the leaf map supplies the leaf clause. At a paired embedding, a smaller sharp neighbourhood is a paired embedding of smaller children. The inductive hypotheses keep the intermediate targets, and monotonicity of the node map enlarges the final target.
